# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies / build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
# No `lib/` rule.
#
# It was here for build output, and nothing in this repository emits to `lib/`
# — every TypeScript project compiles to `dist/`. What it did instead was
# exclude three directories of source: apps/mobile/src/lib (the API client,
# telemetry and query client that every screen imports), scripts/aws/lib and
# scripts/bootstrap/lib (the shell libraries every operational script sources).
#
# A clean clone therefore could not typecheck the mobile app at all — it failed
# with "Cannot find module '@/lib/api'" on twelve files — and could not run the
# bootstrap scripts either. It went unnoticed because the files exist locally,
# so everything worked for the one person who had them.
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expo / React Native
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.expo/
.expo-shared/
*.jsbundle
apps/mobile/ios/build/
apps/mobile/ios/Pods/
apps/mobile/ios/.xcode.env.local
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
# CocoaPods install output. `expo prebuild --clean` wipes and regenerates ios/,
# so committing anything `pod install` produced means the next prebuild deletes
# it and the diff never settles. `pod install` runs before every real build —
# EAS does it, and `pnpm --filter @family/mobile pods` does it locally — so
# these exist when they need to, including the privacy manifest Apple requires
# in the shipped app.
apps/mobile/ios/Podfile.lock
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/
apps/mobile/ios/*/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
apps/mobile/android/.gradle/
apps/mobile/android/build/
apps/mobile/android/app/build/
apps/mobile/android/local.properties
apps/mobile/android/.cxx/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS CDK
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cdk.out/
cdk.context.json
.cdk.staging/

